    description: "FOUND by WI-tusad F2 (finding 8). tree-sitter-v lexes any one-capital name as a generic placeholder. F2 recovers `struct A {}`, `enum E`, `interface I` from the ERROR node (_recover_single_letter_type), but a one-letter type alias (`type A = int`) still does not parse and is not recovered; V emits no alias kind at all, so nothing is lost relative to multi-letter aliases today, but the alias kind gap and the grammar bug both stand. Fix path: emit V type aliases (kind `type`) and extend the recovery to `type X = ...`, or bump/patch the grammar."  # 5c35
